 ## Known Issues
 
-- Nvidia dGPU is finicky
-  - Needs option ROM
-  - Power enable code is buggy
-  - Proprietary driver does not work at all
+- Nvidia dGPU (T480, T480s, T580)
+  - Tested on a T480 with a GeForce MX150 only
+  - The GPU has no ROM of its own: add the VBIOS of the vendor firmware to CBFS as
+    `pci10de,1d10.rom` (type `optionrom`), the driver reads it through ACPI `_ROM`
   - Nouveau only works on linux 6.8-6.9
+  - The vendor firmware's GC6 and Optimus `_DSM` methods are not implemented
+
+### Nvidia dGPU
+
+The option `dgpu_enable` powers the GPU in the bootblock, so that it is on the PCIe
+bus when FSP-S looks at root port 1. FSP-S disables a root port without a link, and the
+port then stays disabled until the next power cycle. The first boot after the option
+was turned on therefore does one full reset.
+
+An ACPI power resource lets the OS turn the GPU off (D3cold) while no driver uses it.
+The GPU is also turned off before the system enters S3, S4 or S5.
+
+Tested with the proprietary driver 580.178.04 on Linux 7.2: render offload with OpenGL
+and Vulkan, suspend and resume.
 
 ## Verified Working
 
